  {
    "text": "The post-mitotic nuclear reassembly window is a transient state between chromosome segregation and nuclear envelope reassembly where prior genomic organization has collapsed.",
    "topic": "post-mitotic nuclear reassembly window"
  },
  {
    "text": "A minimal three-variable dynamical model (chromosome separation dchr, nuclear envelope reassembly N, bookmarking occupancy B) has been developed to describe this window.",
    "topic": "minimal dynamical model"
  },
  {
    "text": "The model is calibrated using semi-real, order-of-magnitude constraints drawn from HeLa literature.",
    "topic": "model calibration"
  },
  {
    "text": "Bookmarking factors retain a residual mitotic memory during the nuclear reassembly window.",
    "topic": "mitotic memory"
  },
  {
    "text": "HeLa literature constraints can partially resolve the structural identifiability of the minimal dynamical model of the nuclear reassembly window.",
    "topic": "structural identifiability"
  }
]
